 "prompt": "Model a gusseted L-shaped angle bracket (all dimensions in mm).\n- Base plate: X from 0 to 80, Y from 0 to 50, Z from 0 to 6.\n- Upright plate: X from 0 to 6, Y from 0 to 50, Z from 0 to 60.\n- Inside bend: fillet radius 5 on the concave edge where the base top meets the upright inner face (the edge along Y at X = 6, Z = 6).\n- One triangular gusset, 6 thick, centred at Y = 25 (Y from 22 to 28); in the XZ plane it is the triangle (6,6), (46,6), (6,46).\n- Two slots through the base, 9 wide and 29 long overall (rounded ends), long axis along X, centred at X = 55 and at Y = 12 and Y = 38.\n- Two through holes in the upright, diameter 11, axis along X, at (Y = 12, Z = 40) and (Y = 38, Z = 40).\n- Design intent: slots and holes are 12 mm from the Y edges; the gusset stays centred in Y.\nRequired PARAMS keys: length, width, height, thickness, bend_radius, gusset_thickness, gusset_leg, slot_width, slot_length, slot_center_x, hole_d, hole_z, edge_offset.",
